---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = "Fallen Lineage Update Notes & Patch History";
const description = "Track official patch notes and update history for Fallen Lineage on Roblox. Review development status and real community channels for latest game news.";
const h1 = "Fallen Lineage Updates";

const siblingLinks = [
  { title: "Roblox Codes", href: "/codes", desc: "Redeem new milestone codes added in recent patches." },
  { title: "Class Tier List", href: "/tier-list", desc: "See how latest balance shifts impact character rankings." },
  { title: "Community Hubs", href: "/trello", desc: "Inspect real developer channels for upcoming news." }
];

const lastUpdatedDate = "November 16, 2026";
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  h1={h1}
  siblingLinks={siblingLinks}
>
  <div style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
    <span class="badge badge-amber">Patch Log</span>
    <h1 style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">{h1}</h1>
    <div class="meta-banner">
      <span><strong>Archive:</strong> Official Patch History</span>
      <span>&bull;</span>
      <span><strong>Last Synchronized:</strong> {lastUpdatedDate}</span>
    </div>
    <p>
      Review historical update notices, balance adjustments, and patch changes for <strong>Fallen Lineage</strong> on Roblox.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>Official Patch Notes Status</h2>
    <div class="callout callout-info" style="margin-top: 1.5rem; padding: 2rem;">
      <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-primary);">No Official Patch Notes Recorded Yet</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        The Fallen Lineage development team currently publishes balance tweaks and announcements directly through their <strong>official Discord server</strong> and in-game broadcasts, rather than issuing formal numbered patch notes.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
        To avoid misinforming players with unverified patch claims, we do not log speculative version numbers. Once formal developer changelogs are published, they will be archived here chronologically.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 3rem;">
    <h2>Where to Track Live Development</h2>
    <p>
      While formal patch logs remain unreleased, you can track real-time game changes using the following community hubs:
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-2" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
      <div class="card">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent-amber-light);">1. Official Community Hubs</h3>
        <p>Developers announce in-progress mechanics, balance experiments, and bug hotfixes directly on Discord.</p>
        <a href="/trello" class="btn btn-secondary" style="font-size: 0.85rem;">Check Community Hubs &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent-amber-light);">2. Active Codes & Shutdown Gifts</h3>
        <p>Developers frequently compensate players for server reboots with Reroll Tokens and extra Lives.</p>
        <a href="/codes" class="btn btn-secondary" style="font-size: 0.85rem;">Check Active Codes &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 3rem;">
    <h2>Class & Progression Reference</h2>
    <p>
      Need to verify current class mechanics or check our testing methodology?
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Read through our 6 archetype breakdowns on the <a href="/classes">Classes Guide</a>.</li>
      <li>Check testing status and benchmark criteria on the <a href="/tier-list">Tier List</a>.</li>
      <li>Review beginner survival strategies in our <a href="/guides/beginner">Beginner Guide</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
